      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SINGULAR (5) has been very honest without winning lately and looks well placed to convert after narrow placings at this track and Atherton. The move from BM60/BM62 form into a BM65 is the query, but he gets meaningful weight relief from the 61.5kg carried last start and brings the strongest recent profile. SUPER FREEZE (4) is the obvious danger after finishing third in a BM70 at Townsville, beaten just over a length after being slow to begin, and his earlier neck second in Class 5 company reads well for this. NOTTINGTON PRINCE (3) was plain in Open grade on soft ground last start, but he drops to a more suitable level, has Aidan Holt back aboard and owns a strong record around 950m. LATIN BOSS (1) also comes back from BM70 company and had genuine excuses when wide throughout at Townsville; his Ewan win prior and solid record at this trip keep him firmly in the minor-winning mix.",
